            <ArticleTitle>A case of variant angina with normal coronary arteriogram who developed acute myocardial infarction and cerebral embolism.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>907-14</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of a 44-year-old male with variant angina who developed acute anterior myocardial infarction 2 weeks following demonstration of normal left coronary artery. This experience provides inferential evidence that myocardial ischemia resulting from coronary spasm may progress into myocardial infarction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
